This project is an independent GPUIX port of Pierre Diffs. It is not an
official product of The Pierre Computer Company.

Pierre source, editor algorithms, themes, samples, and playground data derive
from https://github.com/pierrecomputer/pierre at commit
c5b1e58203fa5c59dd99353cbcac09ee653a24f6, package @pierre/diffs 1.4.3.
The original Apache-2.0 license is in vendor/pierre/LICENSE.md. The manifests
in vendor/pierre and vendor/pierre-playground record source hashes and changes.
The native controller adapts Pierre's editor commands. GPUI painting, input,
text geometry, and the React controls replace the browser renderer.

The GPUiX runtime and GPUI are separate dependencies under Apache-2.0.
See https://github.com/erwinkn/gpuix and https://github.com/erwinkn/zed.
Their licenses and the GPUiX third-party notices are in vendor/licenses.

The Pierre theme includes work from Primer's MIT-licensed GitHub VS Code theme.
Its full notice is in vendor/licenses/diffs/@pierre__theme__NOTICE.md.
React uses the MIT license in vendor/licenses/LICENSE-React.
Other JavaScript dependency notices are in vendor/licenses/diffs.

Inter, JetBrains Mono, and Geist fonts use the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
See assets/fonts/Inter-OFL.txt, assets/fonts/JetBrainsMono-OFL.txt, and
assets/playground/OFL-Geist.txt. File icons use the license in
assets/playground/LICENSE-icons. Lucide icons use the ISC license distributed
with lucide-static.

The surrounding UI theme adapts Beautiful UI by Shane Levine, under MIT.
See vendor/licenses/Beautiful-UI.md.
